This uses global document; element === document true -> returns false (not belongs). So stopCallback falls through and tagName 'HTML' -> returns undefined (falsy). So stopCallback(document) is falsy, not explicit false. Original library probably target is document, calls stopCallback(e, document) and would return undefined? Actually with target document, _belongsTo(document,target) returns false too, and then HTML not input => undefined. That means stop callback falsey, okay. Adjust to `toBeFalsy()`.
